From a0330976221f8840ced9170aedfc3a7130d2f5a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:08:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add MAF (minimum average fill) elimination algorithm

Thread a node-selection score through MLFLib so the minimum local fill code
can rank vertices by something other than raw deficiency:

- MLFLib: add `MLFScore` with `MinFill` (the existing behaviour) and
  `MinAvgFill` (deficiency / open degree, isolated vertices first), a
  `scoretype` trait that sets the heap's element type, and `mlfscore`.
  `mlf!`, `genmf_wh` and `mfinit_heap` take the score; the old `mlf!`
  signature defaults to `MinFill()`.
- CliqueTrees: export `MAF()`, with docs and references (Otsuka et al.
  2018; Tamaki, arXiv:2108.07551). Add MAF to the algorithm lists in the
  tests.

MF orderings are unchanged (identical permutations on all PACE 2017
instances with up to 50k vertices, with unit, Int and Float64 weights).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C89gtEiR9iugDdkEq8mStv
