 struct MF <: EliminationAlgorithm end
 
+"""
+    MAF <: EliminationAlgorithm
+
+    MAF()
+
+The greedy minimum average fill algorithm. At each step, it eliminates a vertex
+that minimizes the ratio of its fill to its degree. Compared to [`MF`](@ref), it tends to
+produce orderings with smaller width and similar fill. It occasionally adds much more fill than
+necessary, which [`MinimalChordal`](@ref) removes.
+
+### References
+
+  - Otsuka, Hiromu, et al. "Experimental evaluation of greedy treewidth heuristics on huge graphs." *IPSJ SIG Technical Report* 2018-AL-166-12 (2018). (In Japanese.)
+  - Tamaki, Hisao. "A heuristic for listing almost-clique minimal separators of a graph." *arXiv preprint* arXiv:2108.07551 (2021).
+"""
+struct MAF <: EliminationAlgorithm end
+
 """
     MMD <: EliminationAlgorithm
 
